[gd_scene load_steps=19 format=3]

; Mounted power harrow. Authored in the LOWERED (working) pose with the origin ON THE LOWER
; PIN LINE, the frame HitchLinkage solves against; ground is y = -0.21 in this frame, so the
; tines reach 0.02 m INTO the soil and the rear packer roller rests exactly on it — which is
; how a real harrow carries itself and sets its own working depth.
;
; The tine rotor turns about the machine's TRANSVERSE axis, under a hood, which is what makes
; this machine read differently from the mower and the spreader at a glance: their discs sweep
; parallel to the ground, these tines swing through it. One tine bar is painted the same index
; red as the tractor's PTO stub spline, because a symmetric spinning part reads as standing
; still. NO CollisionShape: implements are visual.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/vehicles/tractor/implements/harrow.gd" id="1_harrow"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://src/vehicles/tractor/implements/headstock.tscn" id="2_head"]

